+# Full study: one-variable Zariski cancellation
+
+## Frozen identity {#fragment-identity}
+
+Frozen statement: for every field k, k[X] is cancellative as a k-algebra.
+
+The authority is the exact member record and provider byte range, not the
+surface spelling alone. The Stage6 continuation is `S6-CLM-00006734`.
+
+## Hypotheses {#fragment-hypotheses}
+
+Fix k with Field k; unfold IsCancellative and fix finite-type k-algebra B plus a k-algebra equivalence k[X][X] ≃ₐ[k] B[X].
+
+These are all of the hypotheses: there is no characteristic, cardinality, or
+reducedness side condition beyond what the algebra equivalence forces.
+
+## Inference {#fragment-inference}
+
+Apply the one-dimensional cancellation closure at the exact frozen root.
+
+This is the unique mathematical composition edge between the typed input and
+the target equivalence; the machine ledger binds it to `A-ROOT`.
+
+## Output {#fragment-output}
+
+Construct Nonempty (k[X] ≃ₐ[k] B).
+
+This output is precisely the consequent of `IsCancellative k k[X]` and is used
+by the root declaration and both semantic transports.
+
+## Bidirectional transport {#fragment-transport}
+
+Both source-to-target and target-to-source transports are the identity on the exact elaborated proposition.
+
+The audit declarations check both implications without local aliases or parser
+extensions. The Master must independently recompute the expression hash.
+
+## Exceptional cases {#fragment-exceptions}
+
+No characteristic restriction; all fields and every finite-type commutative k-algebra B are covered.
+
+The empty exceptional-case inventory is a substantive universal-coverage
+claim, not an omitted section.
+
+## Trust boundary {#fragment-trust}
+
+Only trust-zero Lean kernel replay is accepted; the provider sorryAx declaration is statement authority and is excluded as proof authority.
+
+Worker evidence can nominate a provisional candidate only. Integrated-byte
+validation, semantic-environment recomputation, and final acceptance belong to
